{
  "_README": [
    "Reply templates for the POLpro plaintext channel (services/polpro.py).",
    "The file is bind-mounted read-only at /config and re-read whenever its mtime",
    "changes, so an edit takes effect on the next request: no rebuild, no restart.",
    "",
    "FORMAT: {command tag: [entry, ...]}, where each entry is either",
    "    \"echo\"            splice the request's own groups back into the reply",
    "    [\"TAG\", [vals]]   an explicit group",
    "Values may use placeholders:",
    "    $0..$9     Nth value of the request's FIRST group",
    "    $TAG.N     Nth value of the request's <TAG> group",
    "An unknown placeholder resolves to \"0\" rather than failing mid-request.",
    "",
    "A key may be prefixed with the game's service tag: `MJS:RR` answers only that",
    "game's <RR>, while a bare `RR` answers every other game's. Compound keys such",
    "as `SI+IB` (first group <SI>, carrying an <IB> group) are tried before the",
    "plain tag, and `*` is the last-resort fallback. Every outbound code needs its",
    "own entry (`ER`, `BR`, `SI`, `BH`): one that falls to `*` echoes a code the",
    "client has no handler for, and that screen hangs.",
    "Set POL_POLPRO=0 for capture-only silence."
  ],
